# Production build values. Committed on purpose: every VITE_-prefixed value is
# inlined into the browser bundle, so these are public the moment the site
# ships. Never put a secret here — that rule is the same as .env.local's.
#
# Why this file exists at all: `npx convex dev` REWRITES .env.local, pointing
# VITE_CONVEX_URL back at the dev deployment every time it runs. Before this
# file existed, a build made after a dev session silently shipped an /app that
# talked to the dev deployment — which is how packs ended up being saved
# somewhere the CLI can reset.
#
# Vite loads .env.local first and .env.[mode] second, and the later file wins,
# so `vite build` takes these values while `vite`/`convex dev` keeps using
# .env.local. Both workflows stay correct without anyone remembering to switch.

VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://stoic-falcon-22.convex.cloud
VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://stoic-falcon-22.convex.site
